    "reading": "Removing a 32-dim discriminative subspace drives control-vs-tile separability 0.9156 -> 0.6823 (below plain GC's 0.7641) while costing the atlas channel only 0.0080 beyond the capacity price of deleting any 32 of 128 dims. So the signal predicting promoter STRENGTH is substantially not the signal detecting whether a region is regulatory at all.",
