    "subspace_sweep_was_NOT_pre_registered": "The frozen bar specified the 1-D cell only. The k-sweep is corroboration and does not change the verdict label; a frozen bar is not re-specified after a result. It was run because the 1-D cell was underpowered BY CONSTRUCTION -- separability 0.9156 against a 1-D removal cost of -0.0019 is only consistent with a distributed signal.",
    "the_conditional_is_resolved_AGAINST_the_benign_reading": "The limit said 'IF those are upstream-of-gene regions'. They ARE: the authors' own extract_promoter_regions (src/promoter_atlas/utils/genomics.py:6) and extract_promoter_regions_genbank (src/promoter_atlas/io/genbank_io.py:57) take the 200 bp immediately upstream of each annotated gene start, strand-aware, min 5 bp intergenic. So the exposure MECHANISM is live, not hypothetical.",
    "verdict": "EXPOSURE_EXCLUDED_LINEAR",
    "which_clause_of_honest_limit_1_WAS_FALSE": "'separating it needs the corpus sequences (a 2.3 GB h5, or the 3,371 FASTAs), which were not downloaded'. Both halves are wrong. The h5 holds only a one-hot `sequences` array plus a `total_sequences` attribute -- no coordinates, no gene names, no provenance -- so it could never have answered the question. What answered it: 138 lines of the authors' own source, plus the 1,406 control sequences (936 random + 470 neg_control, all exactly 150 bp) that were already in the substrate and are discarded by every arm on this rung via `category == 'tile'`."
